  "originalQuery": "Your company is developing a real-time analytics application on Google Cloud Platform (GCP) that requires low-latency processing of a high volume of streaming data. The current workload is 50,000 events per second (EPS), and you expect this to increase to 150,000 EPS over the next two years. The database solution must accommodate the current workload and scale to meet future requirements. Which of the following options is the most appropriate choice?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Migrate the database to Cloud Datastore and enable automatic scaling.<br/>B. Deploy Cloud Spanner with a multi-regional instance and use partitioned tables to distribute the data.<br/>C. Use Cloud Bigtable with a replication factor of 3 and enable autoscaling based on the workload.<br/>D. Use Cloud SQL with read replicas and increase the instance size when needed.",
  "domain": "Design scalable and highly available cloud database solutions",
  "hasImage": false,
  "queryImage": "",
  "queryImages": [],
  "deprecatedReference": false,
  "deprecatedMatches": {},
  "qid": "257",
  "tip": "<p>Match the workload to the storage model. For sustained <i>write heavy</i> ingestion with <i>low latency</i> and linear <i>horizontal scaling</i>, favor Cloud Bigtable. If you see strong consistency across regions or SQL transactions as primary needs, then consider Cloud Spanner instead.</p>",
